    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_multisource_problem_solving_discourse_management",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-multisource-problem-solving-01",
        "slug": "c1-multisource-problem-solving-discourse-management",
        "title": "Managing complex discourse",
        "rule_summary": "Use signposting and metadiscourse to frame, sequence, return to, and close complex points without losing the listener.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با signposting و metadiscourse نکات پیچیده را قاب‌بندی، مرتب، دوباره جمع و نتیجه‌گیری می‌کنیم تا شنونده مسیر بحث را گم نکند."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Before I come back to that point, let me clarify one assumption.",
            "fa": "قبل از اینکه به آن نکته برگردم، بگذار یک فرض را روشن کنم."
          },
          {
            "en": "That brings us to the broader question of accountability.",
            "fa": "این ما را به پرسش گسترده‌تر پاسخ‌گویی می‌رساند."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_multisource_problem_solving_mixed_conditionals",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-multisource-problem-solving-02",
        "slug": "c1-multisource-problem-solving-mixed-conditionals",
        "title": "Mixed conditionals",
        "rule_summary": "Combine different time references when a past condition has a present result or a present state explains a past outcome.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "وقتی شرط و نتیجه به زمان‌های متفاوت مربوط‌اند از mixed conditional استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "If we had invested earlier, we would be in a stronger position now.",
            "fa": "اگر زودتر سرمایه‌گذاری کرده بودیم، الان موقعیت قوی‌تری داشتیم."
          },
          {
            "en": "If she were less cautious, she might have accepted the offer.",
            "fa": "اگر این‌قدر محتاط نبود، شاید پیشنهاد را قبول کرده بود."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_multisource_problem_solving_advanced_reporting",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-multisource-problem-solving-03",
        "slug": "c1-multisource-problem-solving-advanced-reporting",
        "title": "Advanced reporting verbs",
        "rule_summary": "Choose reporting verbs such as acknowledge, maintain, concede, dispute, imply, and caution to represent a source's stance accurately.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای بازتاب دقیق موضع منبع از فعل‌هایی مثل acknowledge، maintain، concede، dispute، imply و caution استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The author acknowledges the limitation but maintains that the trend is meaningful.",
            "fa": "نویسنده محدودیت را می‌پذیرد اما همچنان معتقد است روند معنادار است."
          },
          {
            "en": "The report cautions against treating correlation as proof of cause.",
            "fa": "گزارش هشدار می‌دهد همبستگی را به‌عنوان اثبات علت در نظر نگیریم."
          }
